+// A diagnostic for the ASTC blocks this driver draws as the error colour, magenta (all-zero blocks, HDR blocks, blocks that are no ASTC data): an upload from guest storage
+// takes them out (astc_clean), a copy does not. Where they come from and where they are:
+// 1. Every copy with an ASTC texture on either side (texture → texture, buffer → texture, WriteTexels) is logged once per kind, textures and levels, and each image's
+//    state once; every 900 frames, how many copies each of those took since and the destination layers they wrote.
+// 2. A scan, every 600 frames, of what the ASTC images those copies touch hold and how the device samples them ("The scan" below).
+// DM_VK_COPY_AUDIT_LINES (default 4000) bounds the scan's lines. Not for play: it reads the images back
